# 6. Persistence Layer

The repo should include a dedicated persistence structure.

Recommended folders:

```text
/system
  /state
  /logs
  /reports
  /runs
  /memory
  /queues
  /decisions
  /validators
```

Recommended files:

```text
/system/state/seedril.sqlite
/system/logs/runs.jsonl
/system/logs/errors.jsonl
/system/memory/seedril_memory.md
/system/queues/inbox.md
/system/queues/next_actions.md
/system/decisions/decision_log.md
/system/reports/daily_repo_report.md
/system/reports/weekly_system_report.md
```

Seedril should use three kinds of memory:

## 6.1 Structured State

Stored in SQLite.

Used for:

* Run IDs
* Timestamps
* Workflow names
* Status
* Inputs
* Outputs
* Error classes
* Retry count
* Linked files
* Human approval status

## 6.2 Append-Only Logs

Stored as JSONL.

Used for:

* Raw event history
* Debugging
* Audit trail
* Recovery after failure

## 6.3 Narrative Memory

Stored as markdown.

Used for:

* Human-readable continuity
* System intent
* Lessons learned
* Current operating posture
* “What Seedril believes is happening”

This prevents the repo from becoming a haunted junk drawer.

