# 10. Validation and Quality System

Quality should be built into the repo as a normal part of output generation.

Recommended validators:

```text
markdownlint
prettier
shellcheck
yamllint
jsonlint
ruff
pytest
actionlint
lychee or markdown-link-check
gitleaks
hadolint
```

Quality tests should check:

* Markdown structure
* Broken links
* Duplicate headings
* Invalid YAML
* Broken JSON
* Shell script safety
* Python formatting
* Secret leakage
* Missing changelogs
* Stale TODOs
* Empty or low-quality reports
* Failed automations
* Repeated unresolved errors

Seedril should not merely generate. Seedril should inspect.

Output quantity without validators becomes mulch.

---

# 11. Output Scaling

The system should increase output by creating recurring production lanes.

Recommended production lanes:

## Daily

* Repo health summary
* Open issue digest
* Stale file scan
* Failed workflow review
* Memory update
* Next-action packet

## Weekly

* System report
* Skill performance report
* Dependency review
* Documentation drift report
* Archive and cleanup proposal
* “What changed this week?” summary

## On Demand

* Convert notes into issues
* Convert issue into implementation plan
* Convert implementation into test checklist
* Convert completed work into changelog
* Convert changelog into release note
* Convert rough concept into source doc

Every lane should produce durable output.

