# 16. Seedril Growth Path

Seedril should grow through phases.

## Phase 1: Scribe

Seedril records runs, summarizes results, updates memory, and identifies next actions.

## Phase 2: Reviewer

Seedril checks outputs against validators, quality standards, stale files, missing tests, and drift.

## Phase 3: Packager

Seedril turns messy notes into clean artifacts: issues, reports, docs, plans, PR drafts, changelogs.

## Phase 4: Coordinator

Seedril routes work between tools: GitHub Actions, n8n, local scripts, Claude Code, notifications, and human review.

## Phase 5: Limited Operator

Seedril can safely execute approved low-risk actions.

## Phase 6: Autonomous Steward

Seedril manages recurring workflows, proposes improvements, maintains memory, and escalates only when needed.

The long-term goal is for Seedril to absorb as many orchestration and maintenance roles as possible while Ember remains builder, guardian, and escalation point.

